  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Source-backed Gateway; external Native contract",
      "items": [
        "Every node cites committed Gateway source at 5e065e84. External Native nodes show the public capability/receipt boundary consumed by Gateway, not Native implementation verified in this repository.",
        "Prepare starts nothing. Encoding and queue reservation precede the atomic possible-send decision. The actual write and response acceptance recheck current rights and immutable identity; duplicate confirmation observes the original operation.",
        "New execution requires fresh live project context and current local ceilings. Passive task controls use frozen receipt guards; namespace operations use fresh root-only evidence without granting project readiness. Both namespace-admission-v1 and namespace-mutation-lease-v1 are required; Native prerequisite 62b11d34 is reviewed separately in PR 179."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "No synthetic task closure",
      "items": [
        "Rows are separate related procedures, not automatic transitions. Lost ACK, timeout, disconnect, accepted result bytes and cancellation requested do not prove task closure. Unknown transmitted work retains its execution reservation.",
        "Explicit cancellation first sends Gateway FenceAbsent for the original ID. A complete matching existing receipt is resolved passively, without Native refusal locking, and may then be canceled. Only validated absence or independently root-checked partial preparation invokes the Native refusal fence. Unknown or partial evidence retains the reservation.",
        "Execution reservation release requires validated canonical execution closure, an exact requested-and-terminated stop, or permanent refusal. Result bytes and routing completion do not establish task closure.",
        "Revoked principal/grant/device or stale credential/connection blocks current sends and responses. Already-transmitted work can finish; revocation is not task cancellation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Recovery conserves identity and visibility",
      "items": [
        "Full prior-fleet coverage precedes EVERY routed CLI. Out-of-band operator CLI-only join attestation is frozen to device, credential, boot and exact generation; it does not establish Native task closure.",
        "Persist barriers before inventory. Import root-wide canonical receipts with each frozen project context and exact budget nanoseconds. Attributed and unattributed records share one honest ledger; unowned work stays admin-only and reserved until canonical drain.",
        "Missing coverage, mapping, completeness, regular credential or reopen revision keeps recovery blocked. Recovery-only permits observation/cancel/fence/barrier/inventory after routing coverage, never admit/resume/reopen. Fresh root proof follows reopen before Registry finish."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Two independent resource ledgers",
      "items": [
        "Execution reservations account for uncertain Native work. Routing permits account only for Gateway-routed CLI owners, not operator CLI/SSH/TUI or a local startup probe.",
        "Routing completion is not task completion. Keep permits while CLI Wait/output copiers/owned cleanup remain unresolved. Same-process fenced census or protected explicit drain can settle prior controls; socket closure alone cannot.",
        "Schema 7 phase-4 retention removes only closed routing rows older than the current generation. Active owners, execution reservations and canonical task evidence are not released by compaction."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Candidate and evidence limits",
      "items": [
        "This is a source-backed Gateway implementation candidate, not release approval. Native public CLI prerequisites are separate. Before PR, independent integrated reviews and no known unresolved P0/P1/P2 remain required.",
        "Current test commands, environments, results and remaining acceptance limits are recorded in docs/verification.md. These graphics establish source provenance only; they do not prove installed-provider, public OAuth, multi-network, Cloud or release acceptance."
      ]
    }
  ]
